      "id": "414b7165",
      "agent_input": "Could you please show me the Q3 2026 sales report? I\u2019d like to review the details before preparing a summary.",
      "agent_response": {
        "response": "Here's the **Meridian Analytics Q3 2026 Sales Report** for your review. I've pulled together both the executive narrative and the deal-level data:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcca Q3 2026 Business Report \u2014 Meridian Analytics\n\n**Period:** July 1 \u2013 September 7, 2026\n**Prepared by:** Rachel Kim (VP of Sales) & Claire Fontaine (CFO)\n\n---\n\n### Executive Summary\n- **22 total opportunities** worked by the 3-person field sales team\n- **14 deals won** \u2192 **$1,040,000** in new contract value\n- **Win rate: 63.6%** (above the 55% company target)\n- **5 deals pending** (~$247,300 in potential revenue expected to close by end of September)\n- **3 deals lost** (~$33,000)\n\n---\n\n### Revenue by Region (Won Deals)\n| Region | Won Revenue |\n|--------|------------|\n| **South** | **$468,000** (leading region) |\n| North | $342,500 |\n| East | $117,000 |\n| West | $104,000 |\n\n---\n\n### Sales Rep Performance\n| Rep | Deals Won | Revenue Won | Pending |\n|-----|-----------|-------------|---------|\n| **James Okafor** | 6 | $528,500 | 1 ($115K) |\n| **Sofia Delgado** | 6 | $462,000 | 1 ($105K) |\n| **Marcus Webb** | 2 | $22,500 | 3 ($24.3K) |\n\n---\n\n### Product Mix\n- **Meridian Insights Pro** \u2014 Majority of closed revenue; includes the top deal of the quarter\n- **Meridian DataBridge** \u2014 Strong land-and-expand vehicle with upsell opportunities maturing in Q4\n- **Meridian Insights Lite** \u2014 Smaller deal sizes, primarily from Marcus Webb's territory\n\n---\n\n### Key Highlights\n- \ud83c\udfc6 **Top deal:** Sofia Delgado closed a **$198,000** Meridian Insights Pro contract (D019) on Sept 5\n- \ud83d\udc65 **Headcount:** 15 employees across Sales (4), Engineering (5), Product (3), HR (1), Finance (2)\n- \u2705 **Support SLA met:** All critical tickets (TKT-004, TKT-011, TKT-015) resolved within 24 hours\n- \u26a0\ufe0f **License alert:** SKU-001 (Insights Pro) at **94% capacity** \u2014 procurement review in October\n\n---\n\n### Pending Deals to Watch\n| Deal | Rep | Product | Amount | Region |\n|------|-----|---------|--------|--------|\n| D007 | Marcus Webb | Insights Lite | $7,800 | East |\n| D013 | Sofia Delgado | Insights Pro | $105,000 | North |\n| D018 | Marcus Webb | Insights Lite | $5,500 | East |\n| D020 | James Okafor | Insights Pro | $115,000 | West |\n| D022 | Marcus Webb | Insights Lite | $11,000 | South |\n\n---\n\n### Next Steps\n1. Close pending deals (D007, D013, D018, D020, D022) before Q3 end\n2. Begin Q4 pipeline review \u2014 target **$1.2M** in new ARR\n3. Resolve open support tickets (TKT-013, TKT-016, TKT-019) ahead of customer success calls\n4. License capacity review for SKU-001 and SKU-003 in early October\n5. HR to initiate two new engineering hire approvals with Kenji Obi for Q4 roadmap\n\n---\n\nYou now have the full picture. A couple of things worth noting as you prepare your summary:\n- The report narrative mentions \"three pending deals (~$240K)\" but the CSV data actually shows **5 pending deals totaling ~$244,300** (D007, D013, D018, D020, D022) \u2014 a minor discrepancy to be aware of.\n- Sofia Delgado and James Okafor are carrying the bulk of revenue; Marcus Webb's pipeline is smaller-ticket Insights Lite deals.\n\nLet me know if you'd like me to help draft the summary or do any further analysis (e.g., month-over-month breakdown, product-level pivot, etc.)!",
        "status_code": null
      },
